{"access_note": "Public domain, no login, plain GET works. Item uploaded by a private user, so cross-check text against Google Books or HathiTrust scans (e.g. officialopinion16justgoog covers vols 40, 41, 43) before citing.", "already_covered_by_existing_job": "none", "coverage": "All volumes 1-43 (1791-1982), public domain, with files NNN_djvu.txt (about 1-2 MB each), NNN.pdf and hOCR. I downloaded vols 28-43 and the text is clean enough to grep. Page headers and the index digest allow page citation. Metadata is at https://archive.org/metadata/op-atty-gen", "est_orders_reached": "A few hundred orders named by number, heavily 1933-1948, plus an index-digest listing per volume; the opinions concentrate on PD-ADMIN, PD-CLASS-EVENTS, PD-WAR-EMERGENCY and PD-INDIAN.", "family": "interpretive-authorities", "format": "plain text (OCR djvu.txt), PDF, hOCR", "how_to_map_to_orders": "Regex for 'Executive [Oo]rder' (No. NNNN | of <date>) near revoked/superseded/invalid/valid/abolished. Many opinions cite orders by date only, so crosswalk date to EO number with the existing FR and Wikisource EO tables. Vol 37 alone has about 160 'Executive Order No.' hits and 400 'Executive order' mentions, and vols 38 and 40 are rich as well. Vol 37 has the 1933 reorganization (EO 6166) opinions and vol 40 the WWII-era opinions. Page numbers come from running heads in the OCR.", "name": "Internet Archive item op-atty-gen: Official Opinions of the Attorneys General, vols 1-43, per-volume OCR text", "url": "https://archive.org/download/op-atty-gen/037_djvu.txt"}
{"already_covered_by_existing_job": "none", "coverage": "About 35 items such as officialopinion16justgoog (v. 18, 25, 32, 40-41, 43), officialopinion04justgoog (v. 30). Alternate scans for cross-checking op-atty-gen, plus AG digests (cu31924032488896 covers vols 17-25).", "est_orders_reached": "Same as above (verification copy)", "family": "interpretive-authorities", "format": "djvu.txt, pdf", "how_to_map_to_orders": "Use as a second copy for quote verification. Digests are indexed by subject, which can be used for 'Executive order' headings.", "name": "Internet Archive Google-scan items for AG Opinions (older volumes)", "url": "https://archive.org/advancedsearch.php?q=title%3A%28%22opinions+of+the+attorneys+general+of+the+united+states%22%29+AND+mediatype%3Atexts&fl%5B%5D=identifier&fl%5B%5D=volume&rows=100&output=json"}
{"access_note": "Public, no login. Volume 44 is 2020. The URL scheme is irregular, so scrape the listing page, not a pattern.", "already_covered_by_existing_job": "none", "coverage": "Whole bound volumes as PDFs, with URL patterns /media/<id>/dl?inline (varies), /olc/file/op-olc-v0NN/download (vols 33-38). Per-opinion pages with PDF are at /olc/opinion/<slug>, and legacy PDFs at /sites/default/files/olc/legacy/.../op-olc-NN.pdf. The vol 24 opinion is /file/146326-0/dl?inline.", "est_orders_reached": "Probably a few hundred orders cited, but few lifecycle holdings.", "family": "interpretive-authorities", "format": "PDF (text layer)", "how_to_map_to_orders": "pdftotext each volume, then regex 'Executive Order (No\\. )?\\d{4,5}' with 'revok|supersed|rescind|remain'. Opinions after 1977 mostly address orders 11,900-13,900. Few declare an order ended; expect mostly validity and scope holdings.", "name": "DOJ OLC Opinions by Volume (Op. O.L.C. vols 1-44, 1977-2020)", "url": "https://www.justice.gov/olc/opinions-volume"}
